1
00:00:01,617 --> 00:00:05,957
Now, one of my biggest tasks is completely finished.

2
00:00:07,027 --> 00:00:09,927
I should hold my funeral soon.

3
00:00:17,537 --> 00:00:20,137
What did you just say, Father?

4
00:00:20,407 --> 00:00:22,807
A funeral?

5
00:00:22,807 --> 00:00:25,007
That's right. My funeral.

6
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:26,747
Grandfather.

7
00:00:27,917 --> 00:00:30,187
I've already discussed it with Young Hwa.

8
00:00:32,087 --> 00:00:35,157
The other grandkids, Chief Seo's family,

9
00:00:35,387 --> 00:00:38,957
find a suitable day when everyone can get together.

10
00:00:39,957 --> 00:00:41,097
Father, hold on.

11
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:48,267
I know you have a terminal diagnosis,

12
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:51,737
but how can you talk about a funeral when you're alive and well?

13
00:00:52,777 --> 00:00:55,607
- What do you mean? - Father.

14
00:00:56,147 --> 00:00:58,577
Don't tell me you're going to Switzerland...

15
00:00:58,647 --> 00:01:00,077
for assisted suicide? Oh my.

16
00:01:03,147 --> 00:01:05,017
Excuse me for asking,

17
00:01:05,887 --> 00:01:09,387
but are you by any chance planning a living funeral?

18
00:01:14,757 --> 00:01:15,797
That's right.

19
00:01:16,897 --> 00:01:19,897
I've been thinking about this for a long time.

20
00:01:21,267 --> 00:01:24,607
After I'm dead, people will gather in front of my portrait.

21
00:01:25,037 --> 00:01:28,277
Can I see them? Can I talk with them?

22
00:01:30,447 --> 00:01:32,077
I want to see the people I've missed,

23
00:01:32,447 --> 00:01:35,947
and gather everyone I wanted to share a meal with.

24
00:01:36,147 --> 00:01:38,817
We'll all laugh and have a good time together.

25
00:01:39,857 --> 00:01:43,857
That's the funeral I'm planning, so you all know what to expect.

26
00:01:45,627 --> 00:01:49,467
If you just let me know how many people can make it,

27
00:01:50,127 --> 00:01:52,237
I'll take care of preparing the food.

28
00:01:52,997 --> 00:01:56,867
Yeon Soon, bring your grandchildren and great-grandchildren.

29
00:01:57,607 --> 00:02:00,577
And if there's any food the kids especially like,

30
00:02:00,637 --> 00:02:02,037
let me know beforehand.

31
00:02:03,747 --> 00:02:04,747
Yes, Madam...

32
00:02:08,347 --> 00:02:09,347
Mom.

33
00:02:13,857 --> 00:02:15,687
Mother.

34
00:02:16,227 --> 00:02:19,627
It's not a party. Why are you inviting the children?

35
00:02:19,727 --> 00:02:21,197
Why isn't it a party?

36
00:02:21,697 --> 00:02:26,097
I plan to enjoy that day to the fullest, like a festival.

37
00:02:27,837 --> 00:02:31,007
You two understand your grandpa's wishes, right?

38
00:02:32,537 --> 00:02:34,837
Yes. We know what you mean.

39
00:02:35,477 --> 00:02:38,507
Min Ho and I will handle the preparations.

40
00:02:38,977 --> 00:02:41,077
Yes. You can leave it to us.

41
00:02:41,477 --> 00:02:43,147
Grandfather, you just focus on staying healthy.

42
00:02:43,347 --> 00:02:45,247
All right, I will.

43
00:02:46,017 --> 00:02:48,957
It feels like everything...

44
00:02:49,087 --> 00:02:52,897
is wrapping up nicely, so I'm happy.

45
00:02:53,797 --> 00:02:54,957
I'm against it.

46
00:02:56,027 --> 00:02:57,027
I understand your intentions are good,

47
00:02:57,097 --> 00:02:58,097
Father...

48
00:02:58,327 --> 00:03:00,967
Miracles can happen. You could get healthy again,

49
00:03:01,767 --> 00:03:04,167
and you might hold on for a few more years.

50
00:03:04,237 --> 00:03:07,207
So why a funeral? I can never agree to this, Father.

51
00:03:09,847 --> 00:03:13,417
Do you really not understand what I'm saying?

52
00:03:14,517 --> 00:03:16,787
Please try to understand how Dae Chi feels.

53
00:03:17,417 --> 00:03:21,357
What child would be happy about their parent's funeral?

54
00:03:32,367 --> 00:03:33,497
At first, I...

55
00:03:33,937 --> 00:03:36,367
When you told me in your hospital room,

56
00:03:37,167 --> 00:03:39,577
I didn't accept it easily either.

57
00:03:40,707 --> 00:03:41,877
I...

58
00:03:42,707 --> 00:03:44,247
have an idea of...

59
00:03:44,747 --> 00:03:47,417
how I want my final moments to be, Young Hwa.

60
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:50,887
You told me not to put you on life support.

61
00:03:51,417 --> 00:03:53,357
And that you wanted to have a living funeral.

62
00:03:54,687 --> 00:03:57,187
It felt like you were about to leave any second.

63
00:03:57,257 --> 00:03:58,997
I can't tell you how upset I was.

64
00:03:59,657 --> 00:04:01,927
Everyone...

65
00:04:02,467 --> 00:04:03,927
dies someday.

66
00:04:05,197 --> 00:04:07,337
It's not about how long you live,

67
00:04:08,137 --> 00:04:09,337
but whether during your life,

68
00:04:10,267 --> 00:04:12,137
you can feel that you've truly lived well.

69
00:04:12,577 --> 00:04:14,277
That's the greatest blessing.

70
00:04:16,077 --> 00:04:18,707
I am a very fortunate man.

71
00:04:20,247 --> 00:04:22,077
I've experienced failure,

72
00:04:22,587 --> 00:04:24,317
and I've experienced success.

73
00:04:25,287 --> 00:04:26,317
Most of all,

74
00:04:27,387 --> 00:04:28,887
after meeting you, Young Hwa,

75
00:04:30,157 --> 00:04:32,457
every single day was a blessing.

76
00:04:33,097 --> 00:04:35,057
I'm the one who should be grateful.

77
00:04:36,997 --> 00:04:39,167
If it weren't for you, I never would have...

78
00:04:39,567 --> 00:04:42,307
even dreamed of seeing our Yeon Soon again.

79
00:04:43,207 --> 00:04:45,507
I would've given up long ago.

80
00:04:48,107 --> 00:04:51,877
But you kept your promise.

81
00:04:52,277 --> 00:04:53,617
Did I find her?

82
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:57,017
You two found each other on your own.

83
00:05:00,517 --> 00:05:01,557
Now,

84
00:05:02,287 --> 00:05:05,257
there's one thing left to do.

85
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,097
Once that's done,

86
00:05:10,097 --> 00:05:11,227
everything will be perfect.

87
00:05:14,997 --> 00:05:17,807
I wish he could stay a little longer.

88
00:05:19,107 --> 00:05:20,107
We've barely met,

89
00:05:20,177 --> 00:05:21,777
and he's already preparing to leave.

90
00:05:23,047 --> 00:05:25,147
This must be so hard on you.

91
00:05:26,247 --> 00:05:28,417
Of course. He's the one who saved my life.

92
00:05:29,917 --> 00:05:31,717
And yet, I hated him my entire life.

93
00:05:32,617 --> 00:05:33,717
My mother...

94
00:05:34,057 --> 00:05:37,057
Because I thought he was the one who took her from me.

95
00:05:38,757 --> 00:05:41,997
That's understandable. I completely understand.

96
00:05:42,627 --> 00:05:47,097
When he held my hand earlier, I felt so guilty,

97
00:05:47,567 --> 00:05:50,667
for ever having resented him.

98
00:05:50,807 --> 00:05:53,937
Then you should visit him often and be there for him.

99
00:05:55,207 --> 00:05:58,377
And how about calling him Father?

100
00:05:59,247 --> 00:06:01,777
He and your mother were married for over 50 years.

101
00:06:01,947 --> 00:06:03,687
It's only right to call him that, isn't it?

102
00:06:03,747 --> 00:06:07,317
How could I? I'm not good at things like that.

103
00:06:08,217 --> 00:06:09,527
Then again, I guess what you call him...

104
00:06:09,587 --> 00:06:10,587
isn't that important,

105
00:06:11,187 --> 00:06:13,127
as long as he knows how you feel.

106
00:06:14,527 --> 00:06:15,767
You must be tired. Get some sleep.

107
00:06:19,067 --> 00:06:21,897
Ever since her mom bought her that phone,

108
00:06:21,967 --> 00:06:24,607
Bit Na seems a lot more cheerful, at least.

109
00:06:25,307 --> 00:06:28,207
Does Ji Seon keep in touch with Bit Na often?

110
00:06:29,247 --> 00:06:31,747
I'm not sure, but she's taking pictures...

111
00:06:31,807 --> 00:06:35,147
and videos to send to her mom. She's been so excited lately.

112
00:06:36,217 --> 00:06:37,217
That's a relief.

113
00:06:38,317 --> 00:06:40,757
What do you think will happen? Do you think there's any chance...

114
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:42,017
for them during the mediation period?

115
00:06:43,387 --> 00:06:44,387
I don't know.

116
00:06:45,227 --> 00:06:47,557
This time, I didn't say much to Ji Seon.

117
00:06:48,627 --> 00:06:50,467
They'll figure it out for themselves.

118
00:06:51,667 --> 00:06:54,497
It's not like my getting involved will change anything.

119
00:06:54,967 --> 00:06:57,867
Exactly. You should've done that from the start.

120
00:06:58,567 --> 00:07:00,937
I resented and hated him so much,

121
00:07:01,807 --> 00:07:03,247
but after just one bowl of seaweed soup,

122
00:07:03,247 --> 00:07:06,117
my defences crumbled. I feel a bit empty.

123
00:07:08,347 --> 00:07:10,317
Our Bit Na won't end up like me, will she?

124
00:07:11,647 --> 00:07:13,187
A living funeral?

125
00:07:14,017 --> 00:07:16,727
Yes. He said he's been thinking about it for a long time.

126
00:07:17,387 --> 00:07:21,027
I thought, "That sounds just like Grandfather."

127
00:07:21,497 --> 00:07:23,627
I felt this during the competition, too.

128
00:07:23,697 --> 00:07:25,837
The Chairman is a truly respectable man.

129
00:07:26,097 --> 00:07:28,737
He is. A truly respectable man.

130
00:07:29,637 --> 00:07:32,977
If it weren't for Grandfather, I wouldn't be who I am today.

131
00:07:33,907 --> 00:07:34,977
In that spirit,

132
00:07:35,337 --> 00:07:37,307
I'm going to give Grandfather a gift that day,

133
00:07:37,647 --> 00:07:38,707
and I want us to make it together.

134
00:07:39,007 --> 00:07:41,617
- You'll help me, right? - Of course. I'll help.

135
00:07:41,947 --> 00:07:43,417
Just tell me what to do, Team Leader Ko.

136
00:07:44,217 --> 00:07:46,957
Don't you think it's time we changed what we call each other?

137
00:07:47,387 --> 00:07:49,957
When it's just the two of us, instead of "Team Leader Ko"...

138
00:07:50,257 --> 00:07:54,827
- More affectionate and sweet? - What? Affectionate and sweet?

139
00:07:56,067 --> 00:07:57,827
Don't tell me you want me to call you...

140
00:07:57,897 --> 00:07:59,337
by a cheesy pet name.

141
00:07:59,597 --> 00:08:03,407
Why not? I like them. Besides, I'm older, so you should.

142
00:08:03,667 --> 00:08:04,807
So cringey.

143
00:08:05,267 --> 00:08:07,607
The only one I'd call "big brother" is my actual brother, Eun Hyung.

144
00:08:09,037 --> 00:08:10,207
If "big brother" is a no-go,

145
00:08:10,477 --> 00:08:12,647
how about "sweetie," "darling," or "honey?"

146
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:15,277
Oh my gosh, that's so cheesy. What am I going to do with you?

147
00:08:15,347 --> 00:08:17,317
Team Leader Ko, I never knew you were this type of person.

148
00:08:18,447 --> 00:08:22,317
Wait. We already have pet names. The rabbit and the lion.

149
00:08:22,657 --> 00:08:24,227
I'll call you Hoppy,

150
00:08:24,557 --> 00:08:26,897
and you, Eun Ae, can call me Roary. How about it?

151
00:08:27,027 --> 00:08:30,267
This is really making me want to duel you.

152
00:08:30,327 --> 00:08:31,327
What do you say?

153
00:08:31,397 --> 00:08:33,297
Want to have a kicking contest with me?

154
00:08:33,367 --> 00:08:35,267
I heard you did some Taekwondo when you were seven.

155
00:08:35,337 --> 00:08:37,967
Oh, please. You think I'll back down from a challenge?

156
00:08:38,037 --> 00:08:39,577
Want me to show you my seven-year-old Taekwondo moves?

157
00:08:39,577 --> 00:08:40,707
Take this!

158
00:08:41,737 --> 00:08:44,247
All right, Hop, Hoppy. Come on. Bring it on.

159
00:08:44,307 --> 00:08:47,317
Stop that, seriously. It's not cute at all.

160
00:08:47,377 --> 00:08:48,417
Seriously.

161
00:08:50,387 --> 00:08:51,447
So...

162
00:08:51,717 --> 00:08:54,817
why the main character, Ban Do Yeon, is suddenly acting all cute,

163
00:08:55,157 --> 00:08:56,557
that's what you find weird?

164
00:08:57,387 --> 00:09:00,227
Yes. Based on her original character,

165
00:09:00,297 --> 00:09:01,897
she'd go for days without showering,

166
00:09:01,957 --> 00:09:03,797
and her hair would be a total mess.

167
00:09:03,867 --> 00:09:06,167
She's supposed to be frantically running around the ER.

168
00:09:06,667 --> 00:09:07,667
Excuse me.

169
00:09:08,097 --> 00:09:10,737
People change. Is there some rule our character...

170
00:09:10,807 --> 00:09:12,337
has to be like that all the time?

171
00:09:12,737 --> 00:09:16,477
Maybe she had a change of heart after her burnout.

172
00:09:17,707 --> 00:09:19,177
This isn't going to work.

173
00:09:19,977 --> 00:09:22,147
Just this phone call...

174
00:09:22,247 --> 00:09:23,387
How should I put this...

175
00:09:23,447 --> 00:09:25,747
This isn't enough for us to communicate properly.

176
00:09:26,087 --> 00:09:28,787
Yes, come to the studio. Right now.

177
00:09:29,157 --> 00:09:30,157
What?

178
00:09:31,087 --> 00:09:33,527
You're telling me to come to the studio at this hour?

179
00:09:33,797 --> 00:09:37,197
Our webtoon's release date is just around the corner.

180
00:09:37,267 --> 00:09:39,667
How can we proceed if we can't even agree...

181
00:09:39,737 --> 00:09:42,497
on such a minor detail? Come over. Now.

182
00:09:42,567 --> 00:09:45,037
But the last bus is about to leave.

183
00:09:45,567 --> 00:09:47,877
Now's not a great time.

184
00:09:49,507 --> 00:09:52,077
How about we video call instead?

185
00:09:53,547 --> 00:09:56,047
What? A video call?

186
00:09:57,117 --> 00:09:58,117
I mean...

187
00:09:58,447 --> 00:10:00,817
Should we?

188
00:10:02,757 --> 00:10:04,927
Let's start our meeting again in five minutes.

189
00:10:05,127 --> 00:10:06,227
Okay, got it.

190
00:10:08,257 --> 00:10:09,267
My clothes...

191
00:10:11,897 --> 00:10:12,897
This one. This one.

192
00:10:14,837 --> 00:10:15,837
Gosh.

193
00:10:20,337 --> 00:10:23,207
So, where were we?

194
00:10:24,507 --> 00:10:29,177
Right, about the main character acting all pretty.

195
00:10:30,487 --> 00:10:31,587
That's...

196
00:10:33,217 --> 00:10:34,617
- What are you doing? - What?

197
00:10:41,397 --> 00:10:43,897
What does it look like I'm doing? I was in a video conference.

198
00:10:43,967 --> 00:10:45,267
Then why'd you hang up as soon as I came in?

199
00:10:45,327 --> 00:10:46,397
No, that's not it.

200
00:10:46,397 --> 00:10:50,137
- It was just time to end the call. - Oh, really?

201
00:10:53,407 --> 00:10:55,607
What? She hasn't logged in yet.

202
00:10:56,347 --> 00:10:59,477
- Who hasn't logged in where? - It's nothing.

203
00:10:59,647 --> 00:11:02,017
Hey. I was pretty surprised by Mom.

204
00:11:02,547 --> 00:11:06,387
I mean, most mothers would say wrong is wrong, no matter who it is.

205
00:11:06,817 --> 00:11:08,987
- Isn't that what's normal? - Exactly.

206
00:11:09,287 --> 00:11:12,227
I didn't expect Mom to be so understanding either.

207
00:11:12,857 --> 00:11:15,967
But for a writer, you're not very open-minded, are you?

208
00:11:17,227 --> 00:11:19,097
Was I being that way?

209
00:11:22,867 --> 00:11:24,107
Who was that?

210
00:11:24,567 --> 00:11:27,437
Did someone walk in that made her hang up?

211
00:11:28,507 --> 00:11:29,507
Was it her mom?

212
00:11:30,947 --> 00:11:33,277
But we have to have our meeting.

213
00:11:38,687 --> 00:11:41,057
Okay, Seo Seung Woo, just go to sleep.

214
00:11:41,217 --> 00:11:43,627
Right. If I go to sleep, the morning will come,

215
00:11:43,687 --> 00:11:45,057
and when the morning comes...

216
00:11:45,457 --> 00:11:48,297
we can finally meet in person and have our meeting.

217
00:11:48,997 --> 00:11:52,097
Okay, time to sleep, Seo Seung Woo. Good night.

218
00:11:55,667 --> 00:11:56,737
I can't sleep.

219
00:12:02,477 --> 00:12:04,077
He was part of a voice phishing ring.

220
00:12:04,677 --> 00:12:06,217
His number was in Jung Dong Pal's call records,

221
00:12:06,277 --> 00:12:08,047
so we called to investigate him as a potential victim.

222
00:12:08,247 --> 00:12:09,247
That's a relief.

223
00:12:09,247 --> 00:12:12,347
Yes. She was suddenly chasing a voice phishing scammer...

224
00:12:12,687 --> 00:12:14,557
and was taken hostage. It could've been bad,

225
00:12:14,887 --> 00:12:18,757
but luckily, I was following her. The police showed up right away,

226
00:12:18,827 --> 00:12:20,797
so it ended without major incident.

227
00:12:23,927 --> 00:12:25,167
Twenty-five years ago,

228
00:12:25,567 --> 00:12:27,737
you worked at the branch in Eastern Europe, right?

229
00:12:29,537 --> 00:12:31,707
But even so,

230
00:12:32,037 --> 00:12:33,277
on my first day of elementary school,

231
00:12:33,337 --> 00:12:34,437
I don't understand...

232
00:12:34,507 --> 00:12:36,147
how you couldn't even call to congratulate me.

233
00:12:37,147 --> 00:12:40,247
The man you are today would never have done that.

234
00:12:40,617 --> 00:12:44,947
I thought there was a book of yours I wanted to read,

235
00:12:44,947 --> 00:12:47,317
but I couldn't find it. I'll leave now.

236
00:12:50,157 --> 00:12:51,727
Don't tell me. Did Seung Ri know?

237
00:12:54,557 --> 00:12:56,167
Did she do it to help me...

238
00:12:56,597 --> 00:12:57,997
by going after Jung Dong Pal herself?

239
00:13:07,907 --> 00:13:09,307
He should be sleeping in his bed.

240
00:13:25,427 --> 00:13:29,327
(School Uniform Shop)

241
00:13:40,677 --> 00:13:42,877
(Heart Mailbox)

242
00:13:44,807 --> 00:13:47,017
Something you want to hide and don't want to remember.

243
00:13:47,517 --> 00:13:49,947
But also something you can't just keep bottled up inside.

244
00:13:50,787 --> 00:13:54,057
This isn't for medical treatment or prescription-like counselling,

245
00:13:54,617 --> 00:13:56,727
but a way to unburden your heart through conversation,

246
00:13:56,727 --> 00:13:58,187
an emotional outlet.

247
00:14:01,127 --> 00:14:03,797
(Gangsu Construction)

248
00:14:04,067 --> 00:14:06,497
Yes, Chairman. That's fine with us.

249
00:14:07,467 --> 00:14:09,467
We'll work with whatever time you set.

250
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:11,307
Yes.

251
00:14:13,977 --> 00:14:16,977
- Talking about the living funeral? - Yes.

252
00:14:17,977 --> 00:14:20,877
Now that the Chairman has completed his big project,

253
00:14:21,147 --> 00:14:23,317
it seems he's starting to get his affairs in order.

254
00:14:27,917 --> 00:14:29,927
Is there something you'd like to discuss?

255
00:14:29,987 --> 00:14:32,127
Yes, that's right. I'm here because I have something to say.

256
00:14:32,787 --> 00:14:36,767
I've been thinking about it, and how could you do that?

257
00:14:37,467 --> 00:14:41,067
- Sir? - Even if he isn't your father,

258
00:14:41,137 --> 00:14:43,707
how could you so eagerly accept that funeral on the spot?

259
00:14:44,367 --> 00:14:46,237
I did it because I understand the Chairman's wishes.

260
00:14:46,577 --> 00:14:47,737
Wishes? What wishes?

261
00:14:47,807 --> 00:14:50,547
What do you know about my father, Secretary Jo?

262
00:14:51,377 --> 00:14:53,177
Holding a living funeral doesn't mean...

263
00:14:53,247 --> 00:14:54,947
something is about to happen to him.

264
00:14:55,647 --> 00:14:57,187
Instead, he wants to leave behind good images and memories...

265
00:14:57,247 --> 00:14:58,247
while he's still healthy.

266
00:14:58,787 --> 00:15:01,017
That is the Chairman's wish for his descendants.

267
00:15:01,617 --> 00:15:02,887
Do you really not understand that?

268
00:15:03,087 --> 00:15:04,357
Fine, I don't get it. I really don't.

269
00:15:04,427 --> 00:15:05,427
I don't know anything at all.

270
00:15:06,197 --> 00:15:08,027
And it looks like you, Secretary Jo,

271
00:15:08,527 --> 00:15:11,527
are going to steal my place as chief mourner.

272
00:15:18,637 --> 00:15:19,677
Oh, General Director Ko.

273
00:15:20,477 --> 00:15:23,777
- Is that our Min Ho on the phone? - This weekend? At my house?

274
00:15:24,807 --> 00:15:26,277
I know, I heard.

275
00:15:27,177 --> 00:15:28,847
Okay, go ahead.

276
00:15:31,017 --> 00:15:33,057
Why is our Min Ho going to your house?

277
00:15:33,117 --> 00:15:35,087
Did you invite him over or something?

278
00:15:38,357 --> 00:15:40,357
It seems you two friends are just dying...

279
00:15:40,427 --> 00:15:43,427
to be a part of our family. You're just desperate, aren't you?

280
00:15:43,997 --> 00:15:45,267
One a son-in-law, the other an in-law.

281
00:15:47,497 --> 00:15:50,907
Do you think that by getting tangled up with our family,

282
00:15:51,707 --> 00:15:53,237
my father will just give you...

283
00:15:53,307 --> 00:15:55,437
a position at an affiliate company or something?

284
00:15:57,747 --> 00:16:00,147
Fine. Let's say Sung Jun got where he is...

285
00:16:00,217 --> 00:16:01,417
because of his wife.

286
00:16:02,177 --> 00:16:03,187
But what's your excuse?

287
00:16:04,087 --> 00:16:07,317
Using your daughter to try and hit the jackpot?

288
00:16:07,387 --> 00:16:08,387
You jerk.

289
00:16:08,887 --> 00:16:11,187
What? Did you just grab my collar?

290
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:14,657
Hey, Secretary Jo, take a picture. Get this on video, quick.

291
00:16:14,957 --> 00:16:18,527
I'm not letting this slide. Hurry and get the shot.

292
00:16:18,997 --> 00:16:20,237
Seo Gwon Sik, what do you think you're doing?

293
00:16:20,637 --> 00:16:21,637
Stop it.

294
00:16:27,777 --> 00:16:31,947
I'm going to lose my mind. That jerk. Has he lost his mind?

295
00:16:32,207 --> 00:16:33,417
Is he out of his mind?

296
00:16:34,947 --> 00:16:36,647
Don't you ever speak like that again.

297
00:16:37,647 --> 00:16:39,187
Next time, I won't hold back either.

298
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:43,827
My goodness. Won't hold back?

299
00:16:44,827 --> 00:16:46,957
Have they all lost their minds?

300
00:16:47,457 --> 00:16:48,997
How should I put them all in their place?

301
00:16:49,767 --> 00:16:51,267
This is really driving me crazy.

302
00:16:53,197 --> 00:16:54,197
All right, it's lunchtime.

303
00:16:54,267 --> 00:16:55,897
Let's all grab a bite before we get back to work.

304
00:16:56,907 --> 00:16:58,367
Is it that time already?

305
00:16:58,767 --> 00:17:00,407
We didn't get to have a team dinner after the second...

306
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:02,137
round of the competition, so should we all go out together?

307
00:17:02,277 --> 00:17:03,907
Lunch is on me.

308
00:17:04,107 --> 00:17:06,547
No, it's okay. Jo Eun Ae and I brought our own lunches.

309
00:17:06,847 --> 00:17:07,877
You all should go without us.

310
00:17:07,947 --> 00:17:09,817
No, no, we can skip the packed lunches.

311
00:17:09,887 --> 00:17:10,987
Let's all eat together.

312
00:17:11,047 --> 00:17:13,317
What are you talking about? I don't care about anything else,

313
00:17:13,387 --> 00:17:15,757
but I am absolutely not giving up the lunch Mother packed.

314
00:17:16,587 --> 00:17:17,587
"Mother?"

315
00:17:17,927 --> 00:17:20,797
I guess you call your landlady "Mother."

316
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:25,197
Haven't I mentioned it? I'm boarding at Jo Eun Ae's house.

317
00:17:25,797 --> 00:17:28,797
And this is the delicious lunch that Eun Ae's mother packed for us.

318
00:17:29,337 --> 00:17:30,537
Team Leader Ko...

319
00:17:31,307 --> 00:17:32,567
Eun Ae, is that true?

320
00:17:32,867 --> 00:17:34,607
That you and the Team Leader Ko are living together?

321
00:17:35,307 --> 00:17:36,547
No way. So that's why you two...

322
00:17:36,607 --> 00:17:38,347
have been smelling like the same shampoo...

323
00:17:39,977 --> 00:17:43,417
It just happened by chance. Don't get the wrong idea.

324
00:17:44,187 --> 00:17:48,287
Dating in the open must be nice. You can just flaunt it like this.

325
00:17:48,657 --> 00:17:50,727
Right. Okay, as for the full team lunch,

326
00:17:50,787 --> 00:17:53,527
we'll pick a day for everyone to go together next time.

327
00:17:53,957 --> 00:17:56,057
As it happens, I have something to discuss...

328
00:17:56,127 --> 00:17:58,127
with Manager Seo, so we'll eat together.

329
00:17:58,527 --> 00:18:01,497
So today, Ha Yu Ju and Kim Sung Guk,

330
00:18:01,797 --> 00:18:03,507
you two can go have a nice lunch together.

331
00:18:03,867 --> 00:18:05,637
- Thank you, General Director. - Yes.

332
00:18:05,707 --> 00:18:07,407
- We can get something expensive? - Of course.

333
00:18:07,577 --> 00:18:09,377
- We'll be on our way, then. - See you later.

334
00:18:09,437 --> 00:18:11,777
- Okay. - Manager Seo, shall we go too?

335
00:18:12,307 --> 00:18:13,447
Yes, let's.

336
00:18:14,247 --> 00:18:15,277
Enjoy your meal.

337
00:18:15,277 --> 00:18:16,887
- Okay, see you later. - See you later.

338
00:18:17,687 --> 00:18:18,947
Have a nice lunchbox date.

339
00:18:23,127 --> 00:18:25,887
Well then, shall we go on our picnic?

340
00:18:27,197 --> 00:18:29,257
You're really starting to enjoy this, aren't you?

341
00:18:38,567 --> 00:18:39,877
Here, eat up.

342
00:18:42,407 --> 00:18:44,407
This makes me uncomfortable, General Director.

343
00:18:45,247 --> 00:18:46,617
But you were hurt.

344
00:18:47,317 --> 00:18:49,917
I'm just cutting it for you, so please just eat.

345
00:18:50,417 --> 00:18:51,747
I'm all healed now.

346
00:18:54,687 --> 00:18:55,857
Thank you for the food.

347
00:19:05,997 --> 00:19:06,997
So...

348
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:09,197
are you over the difficult stuff now?

349
00:19:10,567 --> 00:19:12,467
Yes, I suppose so.

350
00:19:13,177 --> 00:19:16,207
You're never going to tell me what happened, are you?

351
00:19:19,277 --> 00:19:21,917
I get it. I won't ask anymore.

352
00:19:23,517 --> 00:19:24,547
And...

353
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:26,247
thank you.

354
00:19:27,517 --> 00:19:30,257
That day we were together, you said it yourself.

355
00:19:31,657 --> 00:19:33,357
That you were just leaning on me for a moment...

356
00:19:33,427 --> 00:19:34,427
because things were tough.

357
00:19:36,827 --> 00:19:38,427
The fact that I'm the person you can lean on...

358
00:19:38,497 --> 00:19:39,497
when you're struggling...

359
00:19:40,437 --> 00:19:41,567
I'm just so glad.

360
00:19:42,467 --> 00:19:43,767
As I said that day,

361
00:19:44,237 --> 00:19:46,637
it doesn't change anything about our relationship.

362
00:19:50,307 --> 00:19:51,347
But...

363
00:19:51,777 --> 00:19:54,977
have you sorted out your feelings for Gyeol?

364
00:19:57,187 --> 00:19:59,687
Can feelings of love be sorted out that easily?

365
00:20:01,787 --> 00:20:04,657
However, his relationship with Jo Eun Ae,

366
00:20:05,057 --> 00:20:06,627
I've definitely come to accept it.

367
00:20:07,397 --> 00:20:09,427
And I know there's no room for me to get in between them.

368
00:20:10,897 --> 00:20:15,797
Really? That's good enough. By the way,

369
00:20:15,867 --> 00:20:17,337
you know your mother invited me over this weekend, right?

370
00:20:18,267 --> 00:20:19,667
Yes, I know.

371
00:20:20,037 --> 00:20:21,877
You're not working that day too, are you?

372
00:20:25,247 --> 00:20:26,677
I guess I'll get to see you on the weekend then.

373
00:20:29,887 --> 00:20:31,917
Hey, did you ask Seung Ri about it?

374
00:20:32,317 --> 00:20:33,357
Ask her about what?

375
00:20:35,057 --> 00:20:38,057
Her sleeping out? No, I didn't.

376
00:20:38,827 --> 00:20:41,027
They're not minors.

377
00:20:41,527 --> 00:20:44,897
If they both chose to do it, they'll have to take responsibility.

378
00:20:44,967 --> 00:20:45,967
Responsibility?

379
00:20:46,537 --> 00:20:48,237
Are you saying my Min Ho did something irresponsible...

380
00:20:48,297 --> 00:20:50,007
with Seung Ri?

381
00:20:51,567 --> 00:20:52,567
I wonder.

382
00:20:53,437 --> 00:20:55,707
What do you mean by that?

383
00:20:56,037 --> 00:20:59,047
Don't be so vague. Say what you mean.

384
00:21:00,417 --> 00:21:01,477
Hello.

385
00:21:01,877 --> 00:21:04,387
I should just quit this line dance class.

386
00:21:04,587 --> 00:21:05,947
I can't stand a single person here. Seriously.

387
00:21:06,047 --> 00:21:09,257
I heard the news. You met your mother?

388
00:21:09,687 --> 00:21:11,087
To think the person Madam was looking for...

389
00:21:11,157 --> 00:21:12,157
was you, Kang Yeon Ja.

390
00:21:12,927 --> 00:21:16,597
- Congratulations, really. - It's nothing. Thank you anyway.

391
00:21:16,667 --> 00:21:20,267
Oh my, now that I look at you, you two really look alike.

392
00:21:20,597 --> 00:21:22,467
The way your eyes are shaped, your smile,

393
00:21:22,867 --> 00:21:23,907
even your elegance.

394
00:21:23,967 --> 00:21:26,107
What's with all that brown-nosing?

395
00:21:26,107 --> 00:21:28,307
She's so transparent.

396
00:21:28,377 --> 00:21:33,077
- Unbelievable. - What are you grumbling, grouch?

397
00:21:33,147 --> 00:21:35,547
What? I wasn't doing anything.

398
00:21:37,387 --> 00:21:40,187
Oh my. Look who it is.

399
00:21:45,957 --> 00:21:47,857
- Welcome, Yong Man. - You're here?

400
00:21:47,927 --> 00:21:48,927
Yes.

401
00:21:49,257 --> 00:21:51,567
Secretary Ju, what are you doing here?

402
00:21:52,067 --> 00:21:55,197
I'm the new member who signed up today. Why?

403
00:21:55,267 --> 00:21:57,207
Oh my, is that true?

404
00:21:59,237 --> 00:22:00,437
Back in my day,

405
00:22:01,607 --> 00:22:03,447
I had some moves.

406
00:22:04,307 --> 00:22:06,747
So I thought I'd give line dance a try for some exercise.

407
00:22:07,747 --> 00:22:11,547
Oh my, I'm speechless. Does Father know?

408
00:22:11,747 --> 00:22:14,087
- That you're here? - Of course.

409
00:22:14,417 --> 00:22:16,787
When the Chairman doesn't have anything special scheduled,

410
00:22:16,957 --> 00:22:19,057
he told me I could work on self-improvement whenever I want.

411
00:22:19,127 --> 00:22:21,257
"Self-improvement." Right.

412
00:22:21,597 --> 00:22:24,227
Are you two a tag team here to stir up trouble? Gosh.

413
00:22:24,297 --> 00:22:27,667
If you don't like the vibe here, then you can go somewhere else.

414
00:22:27,767 --> 00:22:31,537
She is totally Su Jung's nemesis.

415
00:22:32,807 --> 00:22:35,837
I'm getting all heated. It's so hot in here.

416
00:22:35,907 --> 00:22:37,077
- Oh, hello. - Hello.

417
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:38,147
- Hello. - Hello.

418
00:22:38,147 --> 00:22:39,207
Hello.

419
00:22:39,207 --> 00:22:43,217
Excuse me, everyone. He says he's a new member,

420
00:22:43,277 --> 00:22:45,847
but honestly, isn't it a little uncomfortable having a male member?

421
00:22:46,117 --> 00:22:47,517
What do you all think?

422
00:22:48,117 --> 00:22:50,657
What does gender have to do with working out?

423
00:22:50,727 --> 00:22:51,927
That's discrimination.

424
00:22:51,987 --> 00:22:55,527
- What? Discrimination? - How about we put it to a vote?

425
00:22:55,797 --> 00:22:56,967
- You know, democratically. - Sounds good.

426
00:22:57,027 --> 00:22:58,327
- Sounds good. - Sounds good.

427
00:22:58,397 --> 00:22:59,397
All right, shall we?

428
00:22:59,697 --> 00:23:02,897
- All opposed, raise your hand. - Me.

429
00:23:06,707 --> 00:23:09,777
- Oh my, is everyone else for it? - Yes, I'm for it.

430
00:23:09,837 --> 00:23:11,307
- I'm for it. - Me too.

431
00:23:11,377 --> 00:23:12,447
- I'm for it. - I'm for it.

432
00:23:12,507 --> 00:23:14,547
- I'm for it. - All right then, shall we start...

433
00:23:14,617 --> 00:23:16,347
today's class with some fun and energy?

434
00:23:16,417 --> 00:23:17,487
- Yes. - Yes.

435
00:23:18,747 --> 00:23:19,747
All right.

436
00:23:26,287 --> 00:23:27,327
Yes.

437
00:23:40,277 --> 00:23:43,977
- Hey, what are you doing here? - Preparing summer special lecture.

438
00:23:44,377 --> 00:23:46,547
I came out because I have to work until dawn preparing the curriculum.

439
00:23:47,517 --> 00:23:48,617
Wow, that must be tough.

440
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:50,487
Working part-time jobs during the day...

441
00:23:50,687 --> 00:23:53,347
and then teaching and prepping materials at night.

442
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:55,587
My body is tired, but my mind is at ease.

443
00:23:56,117 --> 00:23:57,657
The thought of raising Bit Na with the money...

444
00:23:57,727 --> 00:23:59,227
I earn working this hard gives me strength.

445
00:23:59,857 --> 00:24:02,097
So you're still not going to borrow money...

446
00:24:02,157 --> 00:24:06,267
- from me to get a place? - No. That's not changing.

447
00:24:07,197 --> 00:24:08,597
More than anything, I want to be a father...

448
00:24:08,667 --> 00:24:09,667
that Bit Na can be proud of.

449
00:24:10,107 --> 00:24:13,407
Who's going to stop you? Gosh, so stubborn.

450
00:24:13,877 --> 00:24:14,937
Oh, hey, Eun Ae.

451
00:24:15,837 --> 00:24:17,707
About Gyeol,

452
00:24:18,477 --> 00:24:19,877
it seems like something's wrong with him.

453
00:24:19,947 --> 00:24:22,377
- You haven't noticed? - Why? What do you mean?

454
00:24:22,677 --> 00:24:24,387
No, it's not like that,

455
00:24:25,247 --> 00:24:27,187
but I think he's been having nightmares lately.

456
00:24:27,887 --> 00:24:30,487
He'll jolt awake in his sleep a few times.

457
00:24:32,487 --> 00:24:36,227
It seems like there's something he can't tell anyone about,

458
00:24:37,027 --> 00:24:38,597
and I'm no help at all.

459
00:24:39,227 --> 00:24:41,337
He's your boyfriend, so you should keep an eye on him.

460
00:24:41,867 --> 00:24:45,137
Okay, I will. Thanks, Eun Hyung.

461
00:24:53,177 --> 00:24:54,247
No.

462
00:25:00,887 --> 00:25:01,917
No.

463
00:25:04,327 --> 00:25:07,497
What's wrong, Team Leader Ko? Gosh, wake up.

464
00:25:09,597 --> 00:25:10,597
What...

465
00:25:11,867 --> 00:25:14,037
What is it? Team Leader Ko, were you having a nightmare?

466
00:25:15,637 --> 00:25:16,637
Oh, I guess...

467
00:25:18,337 --> 00:25:19,807
You're covered in sweat.

468
00:25:20,177 --> 00:25:22,377
What could you have been dreaming about?

469
00:25:24,547 --> 00:25:25,577
It's nothing.

470
00:25:26,307 --> 00:25:27,447
You should go back to sleep.

471
00:25:28,017 --> 00:25:29,617
How can I just go to sleep?

472
00:25:30,617 --> 00:25:33,447
Tell me. What was your dream about?

473
00:25:35,717 --> 00:25:38,587
Actually, I've been having the same dream...

474
00:25:38,657 --> 00:25:40,197
for the past few days.

475
00:25:40,957 --> 00:25:42,697
It's a dream I used to have a lot when I was little,

476
00:25:43,327 --> 00:25:45,197
but I haven't had it since middle school.

477
00:25:46,327 --> 00:25:47,867
But it suddenly started again these last few days.

478
00:25:49,297 --> 00:25:52,837
How can you have the same dream for so many years?

479
00:25:54,037 --> 00:25:57,277
Do you think it could be a memory instead of a dream?

480
00:25:58,247 --> 00:25:59,247
A memory?

481
00:26:00,347 --> 00:26:04,917
I'm not sure, but if the same scenes and situations...

482
00:26:04,917 --> 00:26:06,717
keep repeating in your dreams,

483
00:26:06,957 --> 00:26:10,827
maybe it's a subconscious memory appearing as a dream.

484
00:26:13,087 --> 00:26:14,297
Hoppy.

485
00:26:14,827 --> 00:26:18,867
It's late. Go and get some sleep. Don't you have to work tomorrow?

486
00:26:19,397 --> 00:26:21,367
I told you not to call me Hoppy.

487
00:26:21,497 --> 00:26:24,807
When Roary speaks, Hoppy listens.

488
00:26:25,707 --> 00:26:27,137
Fine. I'm going.

489
00:26:28,407 --> 00:26:31,307
Should I sing you a lullaby?

490
00:26:31,877 --> 00:26:32,877
What?

491
00:26:33,207 --> 00:26:36,247
When Hoppy speaks, Roary listens.

492
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:38,387
Okay.

493
00:26:43,117 --> 00:26:44,187
Close your eyes.

494
00:26:49,727 --> 00:26:55,237
On my mother's path

495
00:26:56,037 --> 00:26:59,437
White wild roses bloom

496
00:27:00,237 --> 00:27:06,177
The petals of the white wild rose

497
00:27:06,547 --> 00:27:10,347
Were a tasty treat

498
00:27:13,587 --> 00:27:17,287
Looks like she's pulling an all-nighter at the studio again.

499
00:27:21,497 --> 00:27:23,457
(Heart Mailbox)

500
00:27:23,527 --> 00:27:27,067
(Send Your Heart Here)

501
00:27:27,137 --> 00:27:28,197
(User 1234 Has Logged On)

502
00:27:28,497 --> 00:27:30,707
There she is.

503
00:28:05,707 --> 00:28:08,537
(Our Happy Days)

504
00:28:08,637 --> 00:28:12,147
About my dream. It wasn't a dream. It was a memory.

505
00:28:12,207 --> 00:28:14,777
They say memories can be temporarily erased...

506
00:28:14,847 --> 00:28:16,217
as a defence mechanism.

507
00:28:16,247 --> 00:28:17,287
- My gosh! - What's wrong?

508
00:28:17,287 --> 00:28:19,187
I'll take the clothes to a laundromat and get them dried.

509
00:28:19,387 --> 00:28:20,387
Give me the wet clothes.

510
00:28:20,787 --> 00:28:22,457
- Mom. - Mother.

511
00:28:22,587 --> 00:28:23,587
You...

512
00:28:30,097 --> 00:28:33,497
(Our Happy Days)
